And I think we're getting better

02:45:12.570 --> 02:45:15.030
through the economics of that as well.

02:45:15.030 --> 02:45:18.240
So what it takes to be
able to free up resource,

02:45:18.240 --> 02:45:20.280
to be able to invest in the service.

02:45:20.280 --> 02:45:21.780
- Yeah.
- To have the confidence.

02:45:21.780 --> 02:45:23.160
I think you've seen some of those models

02:45:23.160 --> 02:45:24.593
when you've gone on visits.

02:45:24.593 --> 02:45:25.712
- Mary, did you want to comment?

02:45:25.712 --> 02:45:28.337
- Yes, I just wanted to
say that many of the people

02:45:28.337 --> 02:45:30.135
who are elderly and frail

02:45:30.135 --> 02:45:32.700
actually don't want to go to a hospital.

02:45:32.700 --> 02:45:33.533
- Yeah.
- So actually,

02:45:33.533 --> 02:45:35.040
if we get this right,

02:45:35.040 --> 02:45:37.008
it's about patient choice.

02:45:37.008 --> 02:45:39.781
It's not all being driven by economics.

02:45:39.781 --> 02:45:42.600
I think it's quite important
to just recognise that.

02:45:42.600 --> 02:45:45.780
- Yeah, so any other
comments or questions?

02:45:45.780 --> 02:45:47.340
If not, I mean, Tom, thank you for coming

02:45:47.340 --> 02:45:48.240
and thank you for all you do

02:45:48.240 --> 02:45:50.040
as a National Clinical Director.

02:45:50.040 --> 02:45:52.950
And Amanda, thank you
very much, very good.

02:45:52.950 --> 02:45:54.510
- You can let them

02:45:54.510 --> 02:45:56.136
respond?
- Final words?

02:45:56.136 --> 02:45:57.360
Oh yeah, sorry, do you want to just?

02:45:57.360 --> 02:45:59.483
I thought that was just
comment rather than.

02:45:59.483 --> 02:46:00.722
You want to comment?

02:46:00.722 --> 02:46:01.780
Would you like to comment on that

02:46:01.780 --> 02:46:04.203
or anything else you've heard, Tom?

02:46:05.130 --> 02:46:07.440
- I think the final point
is a really important one.

02:46:07.440 --> 02:46:11.020
You know, what matters to all
people living with frailty

02:46:12.120 --> 02:46:15.930
is predominantly independence

02:46:15.930 --> 02:46:17.380
being at home with family

02:46:18.240 --> 02:46:21.320
and it's so much not about
unnecessary hospitalisation.

02:46:21.320 --> 02:46:22.290
- [Richard] Yeah.

02:46:22.290 --> 02:46:24.132
- There's a lot of opportunity.

02:46:24.132 --> 02:46:26.220
We are hearing about all the innovation

02:46:26.220 --> 02:46:27.240
going across the country.

02:46:27.240 --> 02:46:30.210
We need to systematise that and support

02:46:30.210 --> 02:46:33.123
because there is a very clear
evidence base in this area.

02:46:34.050 --> 02:46:37.745
However, we can codify that,

02:46:37.745 --> 02:46:41.310
but the context is crucial.

02:46:41.310 --> 02:46:43.749
So the way that evidence
base is implemented,

02:46:43.749 --> 02:46:47.560
we're going to provide support to form

02:46:48.420 --> 02:46:51.030
hopefully effective
neighbourhood frailty teams.

02:46:51.030 --> 02:46:52.933
- Great.
- And we will need

02:46:52.933 --> 02:46:53.766
to partner, won't it?

02:46:53.766 --> 02:46:54.780
Broadly in local authorities

02:46:54.780 --> 02:46:56.520
and with communities and voluntary sector,

02:46:56.520 --> 02:46:58.140
things like isolation and so on

02:46:58.140 --> 02:47:00.777
to get older people away
from that environment?

02:47:00.777 --> 02:47:03.660
- Primary care, social care, VCSE sector,

02:47:03.660 --> 02:47:05.400
all have to be involved.

02:47:05.400 --> 02:47:07.590
- Yeah, very good, thank you very much.

02:47:07.590 --> 02:47:09.090
So thank you for that.

02:47:09.090 --> 02:47:12.060
I'm going to move this
on just to the last item.

02:47:12.060 --> 02:47:13.230
So Steve, it's for you.

02:47:13.230 --> 02:47:15.870
It's a further delegation

02:47:15.870 --> 02:47:17.000
of commissioning functions.

02:47:17.000 --> 02:47:18.847
So vaccination screening and CHS.

02:47:19.785 --> 02:47:20.700
- Yeah thanks, Richard.

02:47:20.700 --> 02:47:22.200
Should I'll take the paper is read,

02:47:22.200 --> 02:47:24.030
so I'll just try and
cover a couple of points.

02:47:24.030 --> 02:47:25.980
So the board's being asked to approve

02:47:25.980 --> 02:47:27.694
the proposals in the paper

02:47:27.694 --> 02:47:30.810
and I just want to sort of
add a little caveat to that,

02:47:30.810 --> 02:47:31.920
which is in effect,

02:47:31.920 --> 02:47:34.200
this is not the last
decision the board will take.

02:47:34.200 --> 02:47:35.040
- No.
- It'll be,

02:47:35.040 --> 02:47:37.080
there's still some stuff to work through

02:47:37.080 --> 02:47:38.880
and it'll be subject to a final decision,

02:47:38.880 --> 02:47:40.560
which we'll be very familiar
with having done that

02:47:40.560 --> 02:47:41.610
with specialised
- Yeah.

02:47:41.610 --> 02:47:43.020
- commissioning.

02:47:43.020 --> 02:47:47.760
So a very brief point
on the why around this,

02:47:47.760 --> 02:47:49.350
which is really important.

02:47:49.350 --> 02:47:51.540
So you've heard me say this before,

02:47:51.540 --> 02:47:53.100
vaccination and screening

02:47:53.100 --> 02:47:54.935
sit very firmly in the population health,

02:47:54.935 --> 02:47:58.170
population health
improvement prevention space.

02:47:58.170 --> 02:48:00.570
Vaccination is the second most effective

02:48:00.570 --> 02:48:03.210
public health intervention to clean water.

02:48:03.210 --> 02:48:05.040
The screening programmes in England

02:48:05.040 --> 02:48:07.953
save 10,000 lives every single year.

02:48:09.300 --> 02:48:12.393
And that's great and we
know that we can do more.

02:48:12.393 --> 02:48:14.790
And the reason that we have come

02:48:14.790 --> 02:48:16.603
to the proposal to delegate

02:48:16.603 --> 02:48:19.947
the vast majority of vaccination
and screening services

02:48:19.947 --> 02:48:21.960
to Integrated Care Boards

02:48:21.960 --> 02:48:24.812
is prevention and improving
population health sit firmly

02:48:24.812 --> 02:48:29.790
as one of the key purposes of ICBs.

02:48:29.790 --> 02:48:31.800
And actually, these sorts of services

02:48:31.800 --> 02:48:34.410
should be integrated into
all of the other work

02:48:34.410 --> 02:48:38.940
that ICBs are doing in this space.

02:48:38.940 --> 02:48:40.350
I think it's important to say

02:48:40.350 --> 02:48:43.830
these will continue to
be national services.

02:48:43.830 --> 02:48:47.010
They are consistent
services across the country.

02:48:47.010 --> 02:48:49.170
They follow advice of the joint committee

02:48:49.170 --> 02:48:50.880
on vaccination and immunisation

02:48:50.880 --> 02:48:53.400
or the UK National Screening Committee

02:48:53.400 --> 02:48:55.860
and that will continue to be the case.

02:48:55.860 --> 02:48:58.470
The thing that will
vary across the country

02:48:58.470 --> 02:49:01.050
is how the delivery of them works.

02:49:01.050 --> 02:49:04.395
So the really hyper-local
stuff by which we mean,

02:49:04.395 --> 02:49:07.290
exactly what Amanda's been
talking about actually.

02:49:07.290 --> 02:49:09.776
So where do you locate the services?

02:49:09.776 --> 02:49:12.150
How do you connect with communities

02:49:12.150 --> 02:49:14.280
to build trust and confidence?

02:49:14.280 --> 02:49:17.790
And that's what we want ICBs to focus on.

02:49:17.790 --> 02:49:21.120
So the kind of delivery end
of it, the delivery model.

02:49:21.120 --> 02:49:22.110
You'll see in the paper

02:49:22.110 --> 02:49:24.630
that we are going to retain
some services nationally

02:49:24.630 --> 02:49:25.463
or some functions nationally.

02:49:25.463 --> 02:49:26.760
So that's the tech,

02:49:26.760 --> 02:49:29.193
the technology and the data platforms

02:49:29.193 --> 02:49:32.955
which will be available
for the country to use.

02:49:32.955 --> 02:49:35.656
And some functions of screening

02:49:35.656 --> 02:49:39.408
that we think we should
retain for purposes of scale.

02:49:39.408 --> 02:49:41.699
And you'll see those in the appendix.

02:49:41.699 --> 02:49:44.699
So for example,
commissioning of the provider

02:49:44.699 --> 02:49:46.172
who sends out the fit kits

02:49:46.172 --> 02:49:47.690
in the bowel cancer screening programme.

02:49:47.690 --> 02:49:49.440
It doesn't make sense to delegate that

02:49:49.440 --> 02:49:51.790
because we do it once on
behalf of the country.

02:49:53.970 --> 02:49:57.490
There are some issues that
we just need to explore

02:49:58.740 --> 02:50:00.702
in the context of some of those services

02:50:00.702 --> 02:50:02.490
and functions that will retain

02:50:02.490 --> 02:50:05.640
particularly around bowel cancer screening

02:50:05.640 --> 02:50:07.305
and cervical labs.

02:50:07.305 --> 02:50:09.360
So we'll continue to work

02:50:09.360 --> 02:50:12.814
on those areas over the
course of the coming month.

02:50:12.814 --> 02:50:14.730
I don't think there are
any show shoppers in there,

02:50:14.730 --> 02:50:16.814
but there's some things that we just need

02:50:16.814 --> 02:50:18.633
to complete our work on.

02:50:19.920 --> 02:50:22.251
So in terms of sort of next steps,

02:50:22.251 --> 02:50:26.190
we've already been
working closely with ICBs

02:50:26.190 --> 02:50:28.402
or rather our regional colleagues have

02:50:28.402 --> 02:50:32.250
to consider the right way in
which to delegate services.

02:50:32.250 --> 02:50:36.240
We'll continue to do that
over the next quarter.

02:50:36.240 --> 02:50:38.909
As I said, answer some of
the outstanding questions

02:50:38.909 --> 02:50:39.990
that we've got.

02:50:39.990 --> 02:50:42.690
There's some work to do
around both the HR process

02:50:42.690 --> 02:50:44.281
and how we will manage

02:50:44.281 --> 02:50:48.180
the delegation of the budget to ICBs.

02:50:48.180 --> 02:50:49.950
But again, very familiar territory

02:50:49.950 --> 02:50:51.390
in terms of what we've already done

02:50:51.390 --> 02:50:53.040
around specialised commissioning.

02:50:54.000 --> 02:50:55.050
The delegation will be subject

02:50:55.050 --> 02:50:56.970
to the usual readiness assessments.

02:50:56.970 --> 02:50:59.730
They'll come back to the
board at the right point.

02:50:59.730 --> 02:51:01.980
But importantly you'll see in the paper

02:51:01.980 --> 02:51:03.150
we're proposing delegation

02:51:03.150 --> 02:51:06.240
from the 1st of April, 2026.

02:51:06.240 --> 02:51:09.420
In reality, ICBs are really
interested in this area

02:51:09.420 --> 02:51:10.878
and have been leaning into it

02:51:10.878 --> 02:51:13.706
for some time actually.

02:51:13.706 --> 02:51:15.543
So the paper just sets out

02:51:15.543 --> 02:51:17.880
that we will continue closer working

02:51:17.880 --> 02:51:20.340
with Integrated Care Boards in '25/26.

02:51:20.340 --> 02:51:21.690
We're not going to do
a big legal agreement

02:51:21.690 --> 02:51:23.043
or anything like that,

02:51:23.043 --> 02:51:25.170
but we will work in a different way

02:51:25.170 --> 02:51:27.503
so ICBs feel like we are supporting them

02:51:27.503 --> 02:51:29.328
in the discharge of a function

02:51:29.328 --> 02:51:31.050
that they have a stake in.

02:51:31.050 --> 02:51:33.120
So we'll still be responsible for it

02:51:33.120 --> 02:51:34.800
and we'll be making the decisions,

02:51:34.800 --> 02:51:37.573
but we'll do that in concert with ICBs

02:51:37.573 --> 02:51:41.870
so that it is a bit more joined up.

02:51:41.870 --> 02:51:43.355
That's all, I think,

02:51:43.355 --> 02:51:44.670
I was going to draw

02:51:44.670 --> 02:51:45.510
the board's attention to.

02:51:45.510 --> 02:51:47.148
- Yeah, I've had one question.
- Of course.

02:51:47.148 --> 02:51:48.810
- And then, I'd like
to draw out one thing.

02:51:48.810 --> 02:51:49.980
Let me draw the point out first.

02:51:49.980 --> 02:51:51.757
First of all, for the
board as we consider it,

02:51:51.757 --> 02:51:55.121
you know, this is how
consistent with the delegation,

02:51:55.121 --> 02:51:57.540
further devolution out into ICBs

02:51:57.540 --> 02:52:00.998
which, you know, I think is
a hugely sensible rewiring

02:52:00.998 --> 02:52:03.270
of the way the NHS operates.

02:52:03.270 --> 02:52:04.680
And also just the board would've seen

02:52:04.680 --> 02:52:06.630
that these proposals
would've been considered

02:52:06.630 --> 02:52:08.640
by the Vaccination Screening Delivery

02:52:08.640 --> 02:52:09.870
and Transformation Board

02:52:09.870 --> 02:52:12.450
by the commission
development delivery group

02:52:12.450 --> 02:52:14.400
and also by the NHS executives.

02:52:14.400 --> 02:52:15.660
So it comes to us

02:52:15.660 --> 02:52:17.460
having sort of been scrubbed essentially

02:52:17.460 --> 02:52:20.430
by three different groups.

02:52:20.430 --> 02:52:21.540
That said, the only question I've got,

02:52:21.540 --> 02:52:23.140
which I couldn't really pick up,

02:52:24.350 --> 02:52:27.055
I'm probably reading it too
fast actually, apologies.

02:52:27.055 --> 02:52:28.590
As we've now allocate,

02:52:28.590 --> 02:52:29.423
as we're now moving

02:52:29.423 --> 02:52:32.130
to a removal of the ring fence,

02:52:32.130 --> 02:52:33.360
not removal completely,

02:52:33.360 --> 02:52:35.910
but we are reducing the
number of ring fences.

02:52:35.910 --> 02:52:37.890
As we allocate these out,

02:52:37.890 --> 02:52:40.320
will these remain ring-fenced effectively

02:52:40.320 --> 02:52:41.433
in the ICBs?

02:52:42.390 --> 02:52:45.107
- Do you want me to have a first
go at that Julian then you.

02:52:45.107 --> 02:52:48.153
So we haven't come to a
final conclusion on that.

02:52:49.950 --> 02:52:51.000
We want to make sure

02:52:51.000 --> 02:52:53.520
that ICBs have got flexibility

02:52:53.520 --> 02:52:56.190
and actually there are some arguments.

02:52:56.190 --> 02:52:58.110
Colleagues will often say
we should ring-fence this

02:52:58.110 --> 02:53:01.427
to make sure it's preserved
in the public health arena.

02:53:01.427 --> 02:53:03.060
And I understand that

02:53:03.060 --> 02:53:05.188
and there are also
counter arguments to that

02:53:05.188 --> 02:53:07.440
because ICBs have large amounts

02:53:07.440 --> 02:53:09.357
of resources allocated to them.

02:53:09.357 --> 02:53:11.233
We allocate money for health
inequalities and so on.

02:53:11.233 --> 02:53:13.350
So there's a bit about
joining all of that.

02:53:13.350 --> 02:53:15.517
- So will you determine
that before we go in?

02:53:15.517 --> 02:53:16.823
- Yeah, so what we'll be doing

02:53:16.823 --> 02:53:19.320
is setting an an outcomes framework

02:53:19.320 --> 02:53:20.910
as part of the delegation agreement.

02:53:20.910 --> 02:53:22.200
And I'd rather do that

02:53:22.200 --> 02:53:24.480
and get agreement from
ICBs on the outcomes,

02:53:24.480 --> 02:53:25.313
and then really leave them

02:53:25.313 --> 02:53:26.700
- Okay.
- to manage

02:53:26.700 --> 02:53:28.373
how they do the resources,

02:53:28.373 --> 02:53:30.570
resource allocation rather.

02:53:30.570 --> 02:53:32.070
The only thing just to quickly say,

02:53:32.070 --> 02:53:35.100
Richard, is historically,

02:53:35.100 --> 02:53:39.300
the Public Health Section
7A grant as it were

02:53:39.300 --> 02:53:42.000
was ring-fenced when it was
delegated to NHS England.

02:53:42.000 --> 02:53:44.238
It hasn't been ring-fenced
for a couple of years.

02:53:44.238 --> 02:53:47.100
So just a point of clarity on that.

02:53:47.100 --> 02:53:47.933
- Okay, thank you.

02:53:47.933 --> 02:53:50.010
So is the board, any other questions?

02:53:50.010 --> 02:53:53.190
Or is the board comfortable
to approve the proposal?

02:53:53.190 --> 02:53:55.200
- Makes total sense.
- Thank you very much.

02:53:55.200 --> 02:53:58.830
Very good, so let me
just quickly go around.

02:53:58.830 --> 02:54:00.870
Is there any other
business before I close?

02:54:00.870 --> 02:54:02.470
Any other business from anybody?

02:54:03.390 --> 02:54:04.223
Okay, well thank you.

02:54:04.223 --> 02:54:05.056
Well, first of all,

02:54:05.056 --> 02:54:06.150
can I just thank the board?

02:54:06.150 --> 02:54:07.710
We've been going actually

02:54:07.710 --> 02:54:10.080
with about an 18-minute lunch break

02:54:10.080 --> 02:54:11.460
since 9:00 this morning.

02:54:11.460 --> 02:54:12.630
So thank you very much

02:54:12.630 --> 02:54:15.482
for your diligence and attention,

02:54:15.482 --> 02:54:18.330
and all as always, contribution.

02:54:18.330 --> 02:54:20.876
And also, can I just
finish by thanking again,

02:54:20.876 --> 02:54:23.001
Wol and Andrew.

02:54:23.001 --> 02:54:24.660
We will miss you.

02:54:24.660 --> 02:54:25.800
Well, we may not miss you,

02:54:25.800 --> 02:54:27.561
but we will.

02:54:27.561 --> 02:54:28.936
We will miss you.

02:54:28.936 --> 02:54:31.740
So thank you very much
for all that you've done.

02:54:31.740 --> 02:54:33.390
That closes the board, thank you.

